== Notes ==
* Dying with a respawn item (such as {{i|Dead Cat}}) in the second or final phase places Isaac in the previous phase, meaning Isaac has to fight that phase again. This does not apply to effects that revive the player in the same room such as {{i|Inner Child}}.
* The transitions between phases count as room changes (which means the {{i|Holy Mantle}} shield will re-activate after each phase, for instance).
* The chambers for second and third phases are not considered boss rooms for the purposes of items such as {{i|Blanket}}.
* {{i|Vanishing Twin}} will spawn a copy of Rotgut's first phase. When either of them is defeated, the fight can be advanced to second phase without killing the remaining boss. Second and third phases are not affected except for the fact that Vanishing Twin familiar will remain with Isaac despite having transformed into a copy of Rotgut. After Isaac defeats the third phase of the boss, the familiar will spawn another Rotgut, which will instantly die and drop an item.

== Trivia ==
* Compared to ''Antibirth'', Rotgut's 1st and 3rd phases have a new visual design.
** Rotgut's appearance change was a decision made by Edmund.
* The maggot inside of Rotgut has been nicknamed "Gus" by the developers.
** {{e|Tainted Spitty}}, an enemy which can appear during the [[Ascent]] to reach {{s|Home}}, bears a strong resemblance to Gus in both appearance and attack patterns.
* Rotgut is the informal name for a grade of moonshine that is very poor quality, being poor enough to be deadly to drink.
* Rotgut is the name of a level from ''Super Meat Boy'', one of Edmund McMillen's earlier games.
* Rotgut's current design is supposed to be a {{e|Fatty}} that grew so big that it fused to the floor, according to developer _Kilburn.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/123641386921754625/123961790529929218/839145631779258378</ref>
** He also speculated that Rotgut could be {{e|It Lives!}} having grown massive instead.
** The reason for this design change was due to Edmund not liking the previous worm-like appearance.

== Bugs ==
{{Bug|If Isaac is small enough (with {{i|Pluto}} for example), he can very easily clip through the ground during the Rotgut fight at phase 2 or 3 and enter {{r|I AM ERROR}} room, consequently skipping the fight to Corpse II.
* Dashing through the Maggot in phase 2 using items such as {{i|Mars}} or {{i|A Pony}} or standing inside of it when {{i|Dark Arts}} deactivates can also clip Isaac through the room, causing the same effect.
* This is also possible by using {{i|Suplex!}} against its second or third phase.}}
{{Bug|If debug 10 ("quick kill") is active, Rotgut will repeat its phase 1 death animation indefinitely, preventing Isaac from accessing phases 2 and 3, thus softlocking the game.}}
{{Bug|If  {{i|Suplex!}} is used to kill Rotgut's first phase, the fight will fail to progress as instead of taking Isaac to the next phase touching Rotgut will hurt him.}}
{{Bug|If Isaac has {{i|Flat Stone}}, the tears WILL NOT bounce on the floor in the crawspace-like rooms, forcing Isaac to shoot at very close range and making the third phase almost unbeatable.}}

